# Cloudflare Pages redirects
# Pretty URLs is enabled — avoid 200 rewrites that loop.
# Routing handled by JS in dashboard.html instead.

# The sandbox build ships in the repo (so it can be uploaded to a hub) but is
# not part of the public site.
/sandbox.html   /   302
/sandbox         /   302

# The Android app's source ships in the repo but is not part of the public
# site. Pages deploys the repository root with no build step, so without this
# every tracked file under android/ would be served as a static download.
#
# This works because Pages evaluates redirects ahead of assets: "Redirects are
# always followed, regardless of whether or not an asset matches the incoming
# request" (developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/redirects, checked
# 2026-10-01). The splat makes it one of the 100 dynamic rules, not the 2,000
# static ones.
#
# This is tidiness, NOT the protection for secrets. A keystore or a
# local.properties must never be committed in the first place -- see the
# Android block in .gitignore. Anything gitignored is never uploaded to Pages
# at all, which is the real boundary.
/android/*      /   302
/android         /   302
